after four days of intensifying protests  and widespread opposition from lawmakers  president ivan duque didn't have many  options left but to withdraw his  controversial tax reform  le solicito al congreso i'm asking  congress to withdraw the law proposed by  the finance ministry  and urgently process a new law that is  the fruit of consensus  in order to avoid financial uncertainty  the reform is not a whim  the reform is a necessity to withdraw it  or not was not the discussion  the real discussion is to be able to  guarantee the continuity  of social programs  celebratory casero lassos beating on  pots and pans could be heard in the  capital bogota just minutes after the  announcement on friday duke had already  promised to make  changes to the law removing the most  controversial points  like new taxes on food but in the face  of a growing death toll  looting an accusation of abuses by the  police he pulled it all together  protesters hailed the announcement as a  victory but they still have a long list  of grievances  and say that the protest will continue  there's also labor reform pension and  health reform  the issue of corruption the increasing  violence against community leaders  the protest will continue and we will  not grow tired  some analysts in the country consider a  tax reform necessary to stabilize  colombia's finances and maintain its  international debt  credit but blame the government for  pushing forward the bill  nobody liked the government still could  have prevented  all the pain and all the suffering that  went into the first four days of  protests if it had at least listened  to people if he had listened and  consulted  with the political parties if he had  listened and consulted  with public opinion but they decided  despite everything to go ahead and  introduce the reform  in spite of their knowledge that it was  deeply unpopular some parts of it  the withdrawal shows just how isolated  president duque is in a country  increasingly on edge while he's hoping  to gather support for a revised  tax reform with less than a year to go  before new elections  the political reality on the streets and  in congress  might make it unlikely alessandra  al jazeera bogota
 

